node_modules/
dist/

# `npm run link:dev` junctions these into dist/ so Foundry can load the repo
# folder in place. They are build output, not source.
/module/
/packs/

# Reference material, not source: the card scans, the corebook text and the
# UI studies the design was read from. ~290MB of somebody else's work, none of
# it needed to build. Keep them locally; they do not belong in a public
# history.
#
# `assets/cards/` is the one thing of somebody else's that *is* committed, and
# the line between them is whether it is needed to build. The scans are not —
# nothing reads them any more, now that `tools/fetch-cards.mjs` takes the card
# text from the publisher's own API. The header art is: it is what the cards
# are drawn with. See `assets/cards/CREDITS.md` for what that means, and drop
# the folder here instead if this history is going public.
docs/

*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
